# A block's `fn` with no signature line that calls itself (Jimmy's ruling LS: "Self calling
# local function needs a signature why not?"): a local function that calls itself needs a
# signature line, as a top-level function does, and says so with `no-signature`, never
# `may-not-end`. One that does not call itself has none and generalizes (Type System
# ch. 5, "A local `let` generalizes"); the signed form checks
# (pos/local-function-recursive-signed). The expected text is derived by hand from the
# ruling. Written by Claude on the claude-lowering-wip and claude-bugs branches; subject
# to change.
emit Ui.*
use Ui.*

Total: fn Nat -> Nat
fn Total n:
    fn Go k, acc = match k -? 1:
        ? less: Go less, acc + k
        nil: acc
    Go n, 0

@page: @unit
@page:
    Ui.Label($text=$"sum {Total 4}")
